+```markdown
+| ID | Functional statement | Cites | Evidence that would prove it | Derivation | Tier 1 | Parts | Must pass | Off-host proof |
+|----|----------------------|-------|------------------------------|------------|--------|-------|-----------|----------------|
+| FS-4 | The passage is read aloud | §2 line 9 | audio capture of the passage | [read] | judge-only — audio | | O3 | .github/workflows/ci.yml#read-aloud |
+```
+
+- **Where it comes from.** The TRD author declares the job at plan time, in the optional
+  `Off-host proof` column of the TRD's `## Objectives` table, on a must-pass objective (see the
+  TRD-authoring contract). **The deriver copies that objective's cell onto every criterion row
+  whose `Must pass` cell names the objective**, verbatim, and writes nothing else in the column:
+  it never invents a job, never writes a cell on a row that names no such objective, and leaves
+  the column out entirely when no objective it was given carries a cell. On the spec path,
+  `spec-scope.js criteria` makes the same copy deterministically.
+- **The cell.** One CI job as `<workflow file>#<job name>`, for example
+  `.github/workflows/ci.yml#read-aloud`; blank, `no`, `none`, `n/a` or a dash means none.
